  <ym-title|Common rank purchases \V draft
  correspondence><label|common-rank-purchases--draft-correspondence>

  Parent author, session <verbatim|hairer-codex-existence-20261111>, under
  the confirmed #26 claim through 2026-11-12 16:40 UTC. Pin
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Text:
  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/actual-rank-purchases.tex>. Unintegrated
  candidate, pending independent mathematical and Lean correspondence review.
  No approved review fields.

  <section|Result and boundary><label|result-and-boundary>

  Following the actual Fares/Snow/Powder/Soft route, organizes frequent
  comparison levels on the original family, the joint readout/marked-history
  quantifiers, unique real/unit normalization, cutoff-uniform bounds at each
  fixed comparison scale, cofinal trial selection, and the ordered limit
  comparison used by the canonical finite-rank-kernel-transport unit. Only
  arities \<less\>=2 are required. This does not close actual local reader
  and all-Matched Pupil premises, which are being supplied separately. The
  prose explicitly retains those estimates. The all-spectator Scotia/relay
  kernel comparison is also a separate dependency; finite rank-test
  measurements do not establish it.

  <section|Inspected declarations><label|inspected-declarations>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.richFaresWithPrediction>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Fares.lean>:
    capitalSnow before profile raising, max floor t/L/mu/crossFloor, shell
    \<gtr\>=snows, franchise after block lengths, selected callback
    Family(Issue.trail Y,...), same Makes, Scrim/Foundation, castle, rated
    and warrant. No Roll/Novena alternative.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.{snows,castle,capitalSnow,franchise}>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Snow.lean>: same Binding.world (HEq) and
    literal prices; shell100*(j+7)*L; finite menu eventual membership; max
    shapers/cultivate floor; PreStand/Shops retained under raising; franchise
    quantifier is all families Paid at its enlarged wait, then their Binding
    with the same prices.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Soft.{Vents,revolving,retailers}>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Soft/Postsale.lean>:
    stagewise finite intersections; trim radii positive and \<less\>= old
    radius and1; post-L late coupling gates; Paid.run realizes late stage; J
    monotonicity makes selected levels unbounded; Timing, Ceremony,
    TableReady and Waltz are substituted on exactly that stage/history.
    Preconditions PreStand, Shops and local numerical purchases remain named
    mathematical dependencies.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Soft.{rented,backstage,cast_off,wheeled}>,
    same root <verbatim|Soft/Star.lean>: Metering/Tender/ShowHours/Vents plus
    LanternMarks; follows_prices supplies beta drift\<less\>=s/8,
    commissioned supplies Wall model, timing supplies Tickets; rented
    constructs one Whip/Nylon and Choir for n\<less\>=2. backstage one
    atlas/lead/course/restarted history before all rows.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Soft.{s_supplies,Path_,s_empire,v_paid_factory}>,
    <verbatim|Soft/Diana.lean>: finite intersections on
    Wall.on_demand/boot/procure/forge; actual StampDuty on Y(k), read M.T,
    Heating and all Named lift tests; Stake paid for each requested reference
    representative; v_stir and turnWheel preserve the same invoice.
    Important: this is not a claim that any arbitrary invertible coordinate
    map supplies the marked estimates.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Soft.{v_conditioned,Factory_,Turning_,
    v_culminates,Quota_,Offers_,v_pay_all,Travels_,v_obtain_purchases}> and
    private <verbatim|sold,ticketed>, <verbatim|Soft/Supra.lean>:
    crushed+pedalling to Instance at arity2; warming/launched and
    Perch.covers/follows along same Path_; quota is eventual N then every p
    then one Tested read/course/Ferm before all Names; fixed-k uniform bounds
    and early-N unit defaults; strict depth/width/scale recursion; gap/error
    limits; root coupons from same Ferm and allocation.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Rank.Price.{columns,awake,outward,at_current,reference_size,Tested,
    Tested.cost,Tested.bijective,weightTag,shrink,shrink_min,Solves,solve,
    Representatives,from_labels,Names,series,within}>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/RANK/Matrices.lean>: awake=a_k^(-d)<em|columns;
    factor2 inverse; position weight differs from factor weight; shrink=(sqrt
    beta)^(-1)/theta; inverse shrink\<less\>=2monitor; finite-dimensional
    uniqueness; actual unit and real structure; outward>a_k^d*2sum
    coefficient bound independent of N,p. Checked
    <verbatim|YM.Labels.Frame.scaled> in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Labels/Reference.lean>,
    and <verbatim|YM.Next.Rank.Station.mag/gap> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/RANK/Station.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Rank.Ship.Bill>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/RANK/Screen.lean>: same actual lower
    representation, e\<gtr\>=0, c=d=1 and common allowance for every
