  <section|Reuse, checks and open review questions><label|reuse-checks-and-open-review-questions>

  Read the shared background index and searched rank/projection/purchase
  notes. No new external theorem is invoked. The new arguments are finite
  simultaneous selection, exact linear normalization and ordered-limit
  passage. Existing canonical units supply the local analytical comparison,
  restarted density, connected coefficients, propagation and Haar/root
  estimate. The linear algebra and subsequence constructions are elementary
  and given explicitly.

  Commands actually run: targeted <verbatim|rg>, <verbatim|cat>,
  <verbatim|sed> on the listed source files and canonical manuscript/evidence
  files; <verbatim|git diff --check> (pass before this record). No Lean
  edits, fresh Lean build or axiom replay. TeX integration/build and visual
  inspection are not yet run. This bounded source reading is not a transitive
  proof audit.

  Review should check the exact one-readout quantifier, unnormalized scale
  weights, the source's actual denominator in the root estimate, and whether
  all required local construction predicates are transparently retained
  rather than silently discharged by general coordinate algebra. If a
  source-specific analytical producer is absent from the canonical chapters,
  record that gap explicitly.

